  "ai.caveat": "※ The AI only <em>finds</em>. Suggested codes are based on the <strong>sample lists</strong> (bundled excerpts/examples); once a master is uploaded under Organisation › Master upload, only codes in the master are proposed. Auto-insurance uses NHI procedure codes unchanged, and no non-covered items are suggested for traffic-accident patients. The billing decision belongs to the billing team — check once more in Claims › <em>Diagnosis codes</em> and <em>Auto-insurance reconciliation</em> before claiming.",
  "license.num": "Organisation · Staff roster",
  "license.h3": "“<em>My renewal is due next month</em>” — that phone call stops (면허신고)",
  "license.badgeLaw": "Medical Service Act §25 (의료법 §25) · Medical Technicians Act §11 (의료기사법 §11)",
  "license.badge": "KM doctors, nurses, nursing assistants, physical therapists: 3 years · CME every year",
  "license.blurb": "A medical licence never expires, but the <em>licence renewal report</em> (Medical Service Act §25) comes round every 3 years on a different date for each person — last report + 3 years. Past 50 staff nobody can keep that in their head, and missing one means an <em>administrative sanction</em>. Register the report date and the deadline is computed and flagged 6 months ahead. If the report date is unknown, <em>issue date + 3 years</em> is used and marked “report history unverified” — the <em>licence number and issue date can be read automatically</em> from a photo of the licence (the licence itself never shows a report date).",
