  "license.icsBtn": "Deadlines .ics <span class=\"arrow\">↓</span>",
  "license.caveat": "※ Licence and qualification reports are filed through each job’s central association — <span id=\"lic-orgs\">—</span>. Links go to each association’s main site; the reporting portal address <em>needs verifying</em>. Admin, front-desk and other staff have no reporting duty, show as “n/a” and are excluded from deadline calculation. CME certificates are kept in each association’s system. A login (PIN) is linked to one row of this roster and only the “Director” role can issue or revoke it.",
  "accred.num": "Organisation · Accreditation self-check",
  "accred.h3": "One month before the survey is <em>too late</em> to start (인증 자체점검)",
  "accred.badgeLaw": "Medical Service Act §58 (의료법 §58) · KOIHA",
  "accred.badge": "Voluntary for Korean-medicine hospitals · valid 4 years",
  "accred.blurb": "Accreditation is <em>voluntary for Korean-medicine hospitals</em> — it is mandatory for long-term-care and psychiatric hospitals (Medical Service Act §58-4, verify) and valid for 4 years. Even so, cramming the preparation after deciding to apply ends in <em>findings</em>. Below is a <em>sample self-check (<span data-accred-count>—</span> items)</em> — the real criteria are KOIHA’s Korean-medicine hospital standards. Tick a line at a time and the progress shows on <em>Home</em>; right before the survey it prints as one PDF page.",
  "accred.printBtn": "Print PDF <span class=\"arrow\">↓</span>",
  "accred.resetBtn": "Reset",
  "accred.caveat": "※ Sample self-check (<span data-accred-count>—</span> items) — the latest <a class=\"small-link\" href=\"https://www.koiha.or.kr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">KOIHA</a> Korean-medicine hospital accreditation standards take precedence. “Related tools in this app” are not accreditation criteria — they link to related screens in this app.",
  "shell.infoEyebrow": "About · sources",
  "shell.infoTitle": "Sources · <em>notes</em>",
  "shell.infoSourcesH": "Sources / basis",
  "shell.infoSources": "Diagnosis codes — Korean Standard Classification of Diseases (KCD) · KOICD diagnosis master (bundled table is a KCD-8 excerpt; KCD-9 effective 2026-01-01 — verify · compare against the latest via master upload) · <a class=\"small-link\" href=\"https://www.koicd.kr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">koicd.kr</a><br>Auto-insurance fees · review notices — MOLIT notice · HIRA (심평원) auto-insurance review · NHI procedure list (bundled procedure table is an example · replaced by master upload) · <a class=\"small-link\" href=\"https://www.law.go.kr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">law.go.kr</a> · <a class=\"small-link\" href=\"https://biz.hira.or.kr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">biz.hira.or.kr</a><br>Medical-expense data filing — NTS Hometax standard (items outside PCC simplified data) · <a class=\"small-link\" href=\"https://www.hometax.go.kr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">hometax.go.kr</a><br>Non-covered half-yearly report — Medical Service Act §45-2, HIRA care-institution portal · <a class=\"small-link\" href=\"https://biz.hira.or.kr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">biz.hira.or.kr</a><br>Medical-record retention — Medical Service Act Enforcement Rule §15 · <a class=\"small-link\" href=\"https://www.law.go.kr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">law.go.kr</a>",
  "shell.infoNoticeH": "Notes",
  "shell.infoNotice": "This tool is a <strong>PoC</strong> (proof of concept) for administrative support — never enter real patient data, and always check the original notices and manuals before a final claim or filing. Every download and printout (.xlsx · .csv · .ics · PDF) carries the mark “PoC — not for real submission · demo data” and a <code>_PoC</code> filename suffix.<br>The bundled diagnosis and procedure tables are <strong>examples/excerpts</strong> — upload the KOICD diagnosis master and the HIRA procedure/fee master (xlsx) under Organisation › Master upload and diagnosis cleanup, reconciliation (auto-insurance · NHIS), search and the AI assist work against those tables (public reference data, kept in this browser only). The NHIS adjustment-reason classes and the appeal deadline (notice date + 90 days) are <strong>illustrative</strong>, not real HIRA codes or forms — follow the “needs confirmation” marks. The Patients-area trackers (guarantees · issuance log · non-covered consent) store pseudonymous patient numbers only.<br>File conversion, validation and forms run inside the browser only; uploaded spreadsheets and resident registration numbers never leave it. The workspace is locked with a per-user <strong>PIN</strong>, and stored items holding names or numbers are <strong>AES-GCM encrypted</strong> with the PIN-protected workspace key, in this browser only. After an unlock the session key is stored in the browser (IndexedDB) as a <strong>non-extractable CryptoKey</strong>, so a reload or reopened tab continues without the PIN within the session length (default 8 h) and the idle window (default 10 min) — anyone at an unlocked, unattended browser can use the app in that window, so lock it when you step away. Who processed what is kept in a pseudonymised (****1234) activity log.<br>Two exceptions — notes in the <strong>AI assist</strong> drawer go, after per-user consent, automatic masking and a preview of what is sent, to an external AI server (ai.pb.gurum.se → Amazon Bedrock, Stockholm); nothing is stored on the server or in this browser. The <strong>live intake board</strong> is a public demo written to a shared PocketBase (clinic-admin.pb.gurum.se); card contents are end-to-end encrypted with the workspace key. Details: <a class=\"small-link\" href=\"#\" id=\"info-privacy-link\">data processing (PoC)</a>. New here? Open <strong>▶ Demo</strong> in the menu — fill in the sample data and follow the 7-step walkthrough.",
  "shell.infoVersionH": "Version",
  "shell.backToIndex": "← Back to the portfolio",
